asciicam (0.3.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add ten effect plugins: solarize, sharpen, halftone, posterize,
    pixelate, emboss, equalize, bloom, swirl and nightvision. The
    README lists 29 effects and what each one's parameter does.
  * Every plugin is also linked into the Linux binary and can be loaded
    from memory as "ramfs:<name>".
  * --sandbox runs each plugin in a locked-down child process (Linux).
    A plugin that makes a forbidden system call is switched off with a
    message, and the program keeps running.
  * Native Windows build with MinGW-w64, without make (nb.exe), with
    console raw mode, VT output and terminal resize.
  * Faster: YUYV to RGB conversion uses SSE4.1, and the picture
    downscale uses SSE2 kernels.
  * Fix integer overflow in the effect filters.
  * The build program ./nb builds from source on Linux, macOS and
    Windows. Its e2e test runs the camera-free checks on macOS.
  * The test suite is now plain C. The Python test scripts are gone.

 -- Harshit Dhanwalkar <harshitpd1729@gmail.com>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 13:30:00 +0530
